      tokenomics: "Bitcoin has a hard cap of 21 million coins. New bitcoins are introduced into circulation through a process called mining, with the reward for mining new blocks halving approximately every four years (the \'halving\' event). This deflationary mechanism contributes to its scarcity and long-term value proposition. The current circulating supply is around 19.5 million BTC.",
